    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": ":checkhealth vim.pack blocks Neovim for increasingly long periods as the number of managed plugins grows.\n\n Measured in an isolated environment using tiny local plugins:\n\n  - 0 plugins: 5 ms\n   - 1 plugin: 102 ms\n   - 5 plugins: 443 ms\n   - 10 plugins: 868 ms\n   - 20 plugins: 1.69 s\n\n With my regular 35-plugin configuration, it takes approximately 2.9 seconds.\n\n The health check appears to execute five synchronous Git subprocesses per plugin while validating the lockfile and\n plugin directory.\n\n Steps to reproduce\n\n Save the following as repro.sh, then run sh repro.sh:\n\n ```sh\n   #!/bin/sh\n   set -eu\n\n   ROOT=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\n   trap 'rm -rf \"$ROOT\"' EXIT\n\n   mkdir -p \\\n     \"$ROOT/config/nvim\" \\\n     \"$ROOT/data\" \\\n     \"$ROOT/state\" \\\n     \"$ROOT/cache\" \\\n     \"$ROOT/source-plugin\"\n\n   printf 'return {}\\n' >\"$ROOT/source-plugin/plugin.lua\"\n\n   git -C \"$ROOT/source-plugin\" init -q\n   git -C \"$ROOT/source-plugin\" add plugin.lua\n   git -C \"$ROOT/source-plugin\" \\\n     -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null \\\n     -c user.name=Repro \\\n     -c user.email=repro@example.invalid \\\n     commit -qm init\n\n   cat >\"$ROOT/repro.lua\" <<'LUA'\n   local specs = {}\n\n   for i = 1, 20 do\n     specs[#specs + 1] = {\n       src = vim.env.REPRO_PLUGIN_SOURCE,\n       name = ('repro-plugin-%02d'):format(i),\n     }\n   end\n\n   vim.pack.add(specs)\n   LUA\n\n   run_nvim() {\n     env \\\n       XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$ROOT/config\" \\\n       XDG_DATA_HOME=\"$ROOT/data\" \\\n       XDG_STATE_HOME=\"$ROOT/state\" \\\n       XDG_CACHE_HOME=\"$ROOT/cache\" \\\n       REPRO_PLUGIN_SOURCE=\"file://$ROOT/source-plugin\" \\\n       nvim --clean -u \"$ROOT/repro.lua\" \"$@\"\n   }\n\n   # Populate the isolated vim.pack installation.\n   run_nvim --headless +qa!\n\n   # Measure the health check after startup.\n   run_nvim --headless \\\n     '+lua local t=vim.uv.hrtime(); vim.cmd(\"silent checkhealth vim.pack\"); print(string.format(\"%.3f ms\",\n (vim.uv.hrtime() - t) / 1e6))' \\\n     +qa!\n ```\n\n This reports approximately 1700 ms on my machine. Recreating the temporary environment with different loop counts\n shows approximately linear scaling.\n\n Expected behavior\n\n :checkhealth vim.pack should not block Neovim for several seconds with an ordinary number of plugins.\n\n Independent repository checks could avoid launching many serial Git subprocesses where possible.\n\n System info\n\n - Nvim version (nvim -v): v0.12.5 (neovim/neovim@v0.12.5)\n - Vim behaves the same?: N/A; vim.pack is Neovim-specific\n - Operating system/version: Darwin 25.6.0\n - Terminal name/version: Ghostty 1.3.2-main-81681158b\n - $TERM: xterm-256color\n - Installation: Homebrew (/opt/homebrew/Cellar/neovim/0.12.5_1)",
